# Names that must never appear in this repo: internal project names, client names, folder names
# off our own machines. One per line; blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Copy this file to .gate-private (git-ignored), put the real names in, then run
#     python bench/gate_publish.py --fingerprint .gate-private
# Nothing from this list ships, not even a truncated hash: a hash confirms a guess for anyone holding
# a candidate list. The rule runs where this file is, and every scan says on its summary line
# whether it was on. CI has no copy, so CI runs the key and phrase rules only.
# A name is matched whole and normalised (case, hyphens, dots and spaces do not matter), so
# unicorn-bakery-internal below also catches "Unicorn Bakery Internal" and "unicorn_bakery_internal".
unicorn-bakery-internal
fictional-client-roadmap
